Safe README wording
===================
- "When a Codex worker runs, the harness reads CLAUDE.md from the target
  working directory and prepends it to the worker prompt as a project-
  conventions section."
- "Claude Code workers inherit per-directory CLAUDE.md through Claude
  Code's own discovery mechanism — the worker is spawned with cwd set to
  the working directory."
- "Lessons are stored per working directory and only project-scoped
  lessons from the same working directory are re-injected into later
  workers (global-scoped lessons are reused across directories)."

Unsafe wording to avoid
=======================
- "Each working directory carries its own CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, and
  MEMORY.md, and the worker reads all three." (MEMORY.md is not read by
  the goal worker; AGENTS.md is not read by the harness — it is only
  honored by Codex itself via cwd.)
- "Per-directory memory is injected into every worker prompt." (Only
  CLAUDE.md is explicitly injected, and only for Codex; for Claude Code
  it is discovered by the CLI, not injected by the harness.)

STATUS: partial
REASON: Per-directory CLAUDE.md reaches both Codex (explicit harness
injection) and Claude Code (native CLI discovery via cwd), and project-
scoped lessons are filtered by workingDir and re-injected as a
"LESSONS FROM PRIOR RUNS" block. But AGENTS.md is not read by the goal
worker (Codex picks it up natively, Claude Code does not), and MEMORY.md
is unrelated to the goal subsystem. Public wording must be narrowed to
CLAUDE.md + scoped lessons.
